<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hua County</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Huatai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hua County is a county of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anyang">Anyang</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the old course of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a>. Its ancient city of Huatai guarded a major crossing of the river and was a strategic fortress in the wars of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sixteen-kingdoms">Sixteen Kingdoms</a> period: it was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dingling">Dingling</a> state of Zhai Wei and, in 398, the first seat of Southern Yan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hua-county.jpg" alt="Hua County" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Windmemories · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20241201_Daokou,_Hua_County_05.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
